       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for adults. The labeled prescription maximum is 3,200 mg/day, and 1,600 mg is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some common regimens, depending on what you intended:\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a typical anti-inflammatory dose.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum prescription dose.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** for analgesia.\n- **1600 mg/day total**, if that was the intended daily amount. That could be 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want the original dose, please confirm that it's intentional and give me the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy before it's entered."
