       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 6,400 mg/day has no recognized indication. It's double the maximum daily dose, and doses that high carry a real risk of serious harm, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Taking responsibility for the order doesn't lower that risk for the patient. Your reply also didn't give a clinical reason that would explain such an unusual dose.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a maximum-dose order:** ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or any other regimen within labeled limits.\n- **Help with a different goal:** if you need stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a multimodal regimen. For example, scheduled acetaminophen could go with ibuprofen at a standard dose.\n- **Check for a typo:** if you meant something like 400 mg or 800 mg per dose, tell me and I'll enter it.\n\nIf you think this dose is warranted, such as in a protocol or a special case, please discuss it with pharmacy first. The order can then go in through whatever pathway your institution requires for doses above the maximum."
